  "creator": "NHS",
  "description": "Five floor exercises for the core from the NHS 10-minute series: crunches, oblique crunches, plank and side plank holds, and a reverse crunch. Planks are short 5 to 10 second holds repeated 8 to 10 times rather than one long hold, which suits beginners. Do fewer holds or shorter ones if your form goes. Warm up first with the NHS 6-minute warm-up (nhs-6-min-warm-up) and finish with the 5-minute stretch (nhs-5-min-cool-down-stretch).",
